From: lgautier at gmail.com (laurent)
Date: Mon, 03 Aug 2009 08:42:24 +0200
Subject: [Rpy] Performances when working with rpy2
Message-ID: <1249281744.6351.6.camel@hot-spring>

Hi,

I had a quick look at performances when working in R from rpy2.

The rpy2.robjects layer is predictably slower (hoewever a bit slower
than R than I wished), while the rpy2.rinterface lower-level interface
is faster.
Working with it is *faster than working from R* (about 7 times on the
simple/simplistic benchmark, and up to 14 times when using psyco).

There is a note about that in the doc for the dev version, but most of
it should apply to the released 2.0.x branch.
http://rpy.sourceforge.net/rpy2/doc-dev/html/performances.html#performances



L.




